          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: گارڈ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "گارڈ — gārḍ — \"a guard\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "عمارت کے دروازے پر ایک گارڈ ہے۔ imārat ke darvāze par ek gārḍ hai. There's a guard at the door of the building."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine or feminine, by the person meant."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "گارڈ (gārḍ) is borrowed from English guard."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
