              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "بھگانا — bhagānā — \"to chase off; to drive away\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "گارڈ نے کتوں کو بھگایا۔ gārḍ ne kuttoṅ ko bhagāyā. The guard chased the dogs away."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past, with نے (he or she …): اس نے بلی کو بھگایا, us ne billī ko bhagāyā."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "بھگانا (bhagānā) is built on بھاگنا, \"to run away\", which CDIAL lists under Sanskrit bhajyate, \"is broken\", and its past form bhagna, \"routed\" (CDIAL 9361): this is the form for putting someone to flight."
            }
          ]
        },
